<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Semigallians</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 1290 CE (approx.) · capital Tērvete</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Baltic people of the fertile Lielupe plain who fought the Livonian crusaders longer than any other, finally abandoning their land in 1290.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Semigallians settled the plain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lielupe">Lielupe</a> river in central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia">Latvia</a> and northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Lithuania</a> in the first millennium. By the 12th century they had a network of strong hillforts, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tervete-hillfort">Tērvete</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mezotne-hillfort">Mežotne</a> among the most important, and their land was the granary of the region.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Regional leaders sometimes acted together under a single war chief. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viesturs">Viesturs</a> allied with the Germans of Riga against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanians">Lithuanians</a> early in the 13th century, then turned against them and joined the Lithuanian victory over the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saule">Saule</a> in 1236. Trade along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-dvina">Daugava</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lielupe">Lielupe</a> brought them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and connections with Rus'.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a> fought them through the 1270s and 1280s; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nameisis">Nameisis</a> led a major revolt. In 1290 the last Semigallians burned their hillforts and many moved south into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Lithuania</a>. Their land was divided between the Order and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/archbishopric-of-riga">Archbishopric of Riga</a>, and Zemgale remains a region of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia">Latvia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/semigallians.jpg" alt="Semigallians" width="320" height="251"><figcaption>Image: Dirk Jansz van Santen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_Van_der_Hagen-KW1049B10_029-LIVONIA_Vulgo_Lyetland.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 1290 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tērvete</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Viesturs, Nameisis</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Baltic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Semigallian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/latvia">Latvia</a>, <a href="/countries/lithuania">Lithuania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Semigallia, Zemgale, Žiemgala</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=945&amp;focus=semigallians" aria-label="Semigallians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5186 258 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Semigallians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5506 514L5556 562"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5556 562h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5506 514h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5506 514h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tērvete. <a href="/atlas?year=945&amp;focus=semigallians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
